<title>UK: Nikko Europe to advise on Athens Paper Mills sale.</title>
<headline>Nikko Europe to advise on Athens Paper Mills sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nikko Europe said on Tuesday that it had been mandated by the Greek government to advise on the forthcoming privatisation of Athens Paper Mills SA.</p>
<p>Nikko said in a statement that the privatisation was expected to take the form of an international sale to 'interested parties', with marketing beginning over the summer and the deal closing by year-end.</p>
<p>Athens Paper Mills is the largest manufacturer of paper and pulp in Greece. Its sale takes place under a wider Greek privatisation programme, which includes the Bank of Crete and the state oil company DEP.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6437</p>
